---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import resume from '../data/resume.json';

const breadcrumbLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": new URL('/', Astro.site).toString() },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "About", "item": new URL('/about', Astro.site).toString() },
  ],
};
---
<Layout
  title="About — Syed Ahmed Ali Shah"
  description="Software developer based in Sukkur, Pakistan — full-stack web, Python, applied AI and blockchain development."
  activePage="about"
>
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbLd)} slot="head" />

<section class="page-head">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-left">
        <div class="kicker">About me</div>
        <h1>I like building things that actually run.</h1>
        <img
          class="about-photo"
          src="/images/ahmed-photo.jpg"
          alt="Portrait of Syed Ahmed Ali Shah"
          width="140" height="140" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"
        />
        <div class="about-facts">
          <div><span>Based in</span><strong>{resume.contact.location}</strong></div>
          <div><span>Languages</span><strong>English · Urdu · Sindhi</strong></div>
          <div><span>Focus</span><strong>Full-stack · AI · Blockchain</strong></div>
          <div><span>Education</span><strong>BS Computer Science, Sukkur IBA</strong></div>
          <div><span>Open to</span><strong>Freelance projects and full-time roles</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="about-links">
          <a href={resume.contact.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
          <a href={resume.contact.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
          <a href="/api/resume" data-resume-link>Resume</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="about-right">
        <p class="about-lead">
          Not slide decks. Not Figma files. Things with a URL, a database, and
          someone other than me clicking around in them.
        </p>

        <p>
          I grew up and studied in Sukkur, Sindh — did my BS in Computer Science at
          Sukkur IBA University, where my final-year project was a <a href="/blog/why-my-voting-dapp-counts-wallets-not-people">blockchain-based voting system</a>. That project is basically the reason the rest of my career
          has bent toward blockchain: I got curious about what it actually takes to
          make a system where "nobody can quietly change the record" isn't a policy,
          it's a property of the code.
        </p>

        <p>
          My first real developer job was remote, for three years, at Clear Edge
          Technology in Canada — mostly Django/Flask and PostgreSQL, plus interactive
          canvas work with Konva.js. It's where I learned that the boring 20% of a
          project (migrations, admin panels, deployment, the stuff nobody demos) is
          usually what determines whether the interesting 80% survives contact with
          real users.
        </p>

        <p>
          After that I came back to Sukkur IBA, this time on the other side of the
          desk — as a Software Development Intern in the Department of Electrical
          Engineering, running their <a href="/ojs">OJS (Open Journal Systems)</a> installation, the
          department website, and a pile of office automation nobody else wanted to
          touch. It's unglamorous work, but it taught me a lot about maintaining
          systems other people depend on daily, not just shipping new ones.
        </p>

        <p>
          Somewhere in the middle of all that I got pulled into prompt engineering and <a href="/ai">applied AI</a> — partly through coursework (DataCamp, Hugging Face), partly by
          just building things: a <a href="/projects/groq-ai-chat">Groq-powered chat app</a> and some small ML models. I don't think of AI and blockchain as separate lanes from "normal"
          web development — they're just more tools for the same underlying job, which
          is turning a real problem into something that works reliably.
        </p>

        <p>
          These days I'm freelancing full-time — React and Node.js on the
          frontend/backend side, Python where data or ML is involved, <a href="/solidity">Solidity</a> when
          the problem genuinely calls for a blockchain (which, to be clear, is rarer
          than blockchain Twitter would have you believe). I'd rather ship a smaller
          thing that's actually deployed than a bigger thing that only exists in a repo.
        </p>

        <h2 class="about-sub">How I work</h2>
        <p>Three things I try to hold myself to on every project:</p>
        <ol class="about-principles">
          <li><strong>Ship something a real user can touch</strong> as early as possible.</li>
          <li><strong>Don't reach for a heavier tool</strong> (blockchain, a new microservice, a new framework) than the problem actually needs.</li>
          <li><strong>Leave the boring parts</strong> (docs, deploys, admin) in better shape than I found them.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          I write about what I build on my <a href="/blog">blog</a>, and I recently
          completed Cyfrin's <a href="/foundry">Foundry Fundamentals</a> course on
          testing and deploying smart contracts.
        </p>

        <p class="about-outro">
          Outside of work: I read a fair amount, listen to podcasts on long stretches
          of nothing-to-do, and play games when I want my brain to stop optimizing
          anything.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<ContactCTA />

<style>
  .page-head{padding:72px 0 88px;}
  @media (max-width:768px){ .page-head{padding:52px 0 64px;} }

  .about-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(260px,360px) 1fr;gap:80px;}
  @media (max-width:900px){ .about-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:44px;} }

  .about-left h1{margin-top:14px;font-size:clamp(30px,3.6vw,42px);letter-spacing:-0.03em;line-height:1.12;}
  .about-photo{
    margin-top:26px;width:128px;height:128px;border-radius:16px;
    object-fit:cover;border:1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .about-facts{margin-top:26px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;}
  .about-facts div{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;}
  .about-facts span{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);}
  .about-facts strong{font-size:15px;color:var(--ink);font-weight:600;}

  .about-right p{margin:0 0 22px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.78;color:var(--body);max-width:68ch;}
  .about-lead{font-size:20px !important;color:var(--ink) !important;line-height:1.6 !important;}
  .about-sub{margin:38px 0 14px;font-size:22px;letter-spacing:-0.02em;}
  .about-outro{color:var(--muted) !important;}
  .about-right a{color:var(--accent);text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-thickness:1px;text-underline-offset:3px;}
  .about-right a:hover{color:var(--accent-hover);}
  .about-principles{list-style:decimal;margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;max-width:68ch;}
  .about-principles li{font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--body);padding-left:4px;}
  .about-principles li::marker{color:var(--muted);font-weight:600;}
  .about-principles strong{color:var(--ink);font-weight:600;}
  .about-links{margin-top:22px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;}
  .about-links a{font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:9999px;padding:7px 14px;background:var(--card);transition:border-color .2s ease,color .2s ease;}
  .about-links a:hover{border-color:var(--accent);color:var(--accent);}
  /* Keep the photo and facts in view beside the story on wide screens. */
  @media (min-width:901px) and (min-height:830px){ .about-left{position:sticky;top:96px;align-self:start;} }
</style>

</Layout>
